  "body": "Add qualified, consent-gated phone observations and GPS-only trip capture for #19. Precise location requires trip consent and a matching reviewed context. The active-trip controller starts GPS plus optional visible-screen wake lock; raw motion remains separate opt-in evidence tooling and feeds no incident rule.\n\nCurrent frozen head: `9f87e2c08be8ac9e9324136fd0c4401ad8823bc6`. This preserves author repairs at `4417cf6` and adds post-throttle motion work accounting with an independent raw callback cap, GPS-only composition with the existing Q42 pipeline, and portable reproduction documentation. Withdrawal purges adapter coordinates even after suspension/stop, blocks precise resume, and occurs synchronously before asynchronous queue deletion. Deletion failures remain explicit and retryable. Synthetic global aliases, blocked-diagnostic floods, synchronous denial results, observer rejection faults, timer failures, stream labels and sink transition delivery are covered by the correction controls.\n\nBoth Robert reviews remain authoritative: [5560453602](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/52#pullrequestreview-5560453602) and [5560599386](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/52#pullrequestreview-5560599386). [Complete per-item disposition and portable commands](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/blob/9f87e2c08be8ac9e9324136fd0c4401ad8823bc6/docs/phone-observations/robert-current-disposition.md) cover all five latest blockers, eleven should-fix items, six earlier findings and the motion/upload scope. No review or original failed evidence was dismissed.\n\nNode **24.17.0**: **102/102 author and unchanged recorder checks plus 12/12 complementary reviewer controls pass**. The three new motion-budget regressions fail against frozen4417 and pass here. [Immutable correction receipt and source hashes](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/blob/a9e35aa/review-probes/results/pr52-a5a383f/manifest.json) bind identical source/test trees to this PR head. Untouched historical reviewer suites remain explicitly different: original22 is17/22, contract-v2 is20/22 and lifecycle16 is14/16; the exact accuracy/browser-managed-motion, prompt-wait, code1-confirmation and timer-reason expectations are disclosed in the report. Q52 owns independent confirmation and separately versioned expectations; Robert's confirmation is pending. No CI checks are currently reported.\n\n**Integration HOLD:** the new trip wrapper delegates the actual Q42 pipeline interface and adds no uploader. Q47 has not cleared queue9b53b74's retirement, durable-intent and sign-out/receipt findings, so real adapter\u2192reviewed queue\u2192actual backend upload has not run. Q44 owns that integration and Q46 supplies the isolated signed-HTTP/PostgreSQL fixture. Robert PR74's new sharing/status contract is under separate review and is not wired here; local session-stop is not server acknowledgement.\n\nReal streams remain disabled without physical qualification. iPhone lock/background behavior, matched battery/data cost, real-browser queue durability, delivery and human outcomes remain unproven. Refs #19. Robert retains #18/#21 ownership. Draft; no merge, deployment or issue closure.\n",
